1
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:26,270
Eu...

2
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:31,530
Eu vou vingar o Archer.

3
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:34,150
Apesar de tudo,

4
00:00:36,050 --> 00:00:38,790
ele ainda era o meu parceiro.

5
00:00:41,030 --> 00:00:42,350
Eu também.

6
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:44,860
Já decidi que vou lutar.

7
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:50,420
Se eu não for até o fim com isso, ele nunca me deixaria em paz.

8
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:54,100
Além disso, não podemos simplesmente deixar o Graal intacto.

9
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:56,520
Ele precisa ser destruído.

10
00:00:58,150 --> 00:00:59,890
Eu concordo.

11
00:01:00,690 --> 00:01:06,610
Um milagre que reúne os desejos de todos, mas aceita apenas um,

12
00:01:06,610 --> 00:01:08,810
nunca deveria ter existido.

13
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:10,940
Saber...

14
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:14,460
Mas você estaria de acordo com isso, Rin?

15
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:17,740
Não é o sonho mais acalentado da família Tohsaka obter o Graal?

16
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:22,040
It is, but I don't want some monkey's paw of a weapon.

17
00:01:22,630 --> 00:01:26,100
I never really had a wish I wanted granted, anyway.

18
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:29,290
And smashing it will be cathartic in its own way.

19
00:01:32,450 --> 00:01:36,170
I didn't enter the Holy Grail War for the spoils. Only to win.

20
00:01:36,170 --> 00:01:40,680
To hold my head high as a Tohsaka.

21
00:01:41,330 --> 00:01:42,550
Sim.

22
00:01:42,550 --> 00:01:43,890
É a sua cara dizer isso.

23
00:01:43,890 --> 00:01:46,330
Como assim é a minha cara?

24
00:01:46,330 --> 00:01:49,510
Nem faz sentido!

25
00:01:49,510 --> 00:01:50,400
Muito bem.

26
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,230
Sh-Shirou?

27
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:54,070
O-O que foi?

28
00:01:54,070 --> 00:01:57,230
Ah, pensei em fazer algo para comermos.

29
00:01:57,230 --> 00:01:59,160
Vocês duas devem estar com fome.

30
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:02,030
A pressa é inimiga da perfeição, não é?

31
00:02:02,030 --> 00:02:06,250
Vamos começar enchendo a barriga e avaliando nossas opções.

32
00:02:06,250 --> 00:02:07,910
Sim, é verdade.

33
00:02:08,730 --> 00:02:11,170
Vamos jantar como de costume.

34
00:02:11,170 --> 00:02:14,170
É assim que sempre fizemos as coisas.

35
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:16,360
Acho que você tem razão.

36
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:19,680
Okay, I'll help out.

37
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:14,670
The Holy Grail is at Ryuudou Temple?

38
00:04:14,670 --> 00:04:15,420
Yes.

39
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:18,800
There are three places in town 
where the Grail can be manifested.

40
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:20,420
My home,

41
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,130
Kirei's church,

42
00:04:22,130 --> 00:04:25,200
and Ryuudou Temple on Mt. Enzou.

43
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:29,640
I sent familiars to each, and the one at Ryuudou Temple was smashed.

44
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:34,270
It's safe to assume that flashy gold jerk is setting up camp at Ryuudou Temple.

45
00:04:34,270 --> 00:04:37,310
Doesn't that mean Issei and the others there are in danger?

46
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:38,430
Look at this.

47
00:04:40,030 --> 00:04:43,320
Everyone there was taken away in ambulances?

48
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,520
Right.

49
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:47,520
This means that any interlopers have been removed ahead of time.

50
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:49,340
Shinji's doing, no doubt.

51
00:04:50,130 --> 00:04:52,440
It's the kind of move I'd expect a wary guy like him to make,

52
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:53,940
but in this case, it's a godsend.

53
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:59,090
Ryuudou Temple, though... That will prove problematic.

54
00:04:59,970 --> 00:05:01,610
With its anti-spirit barrier,

55
00:05:01,610 --> 00:05:05,090
Servants can only enter through the main gate.

56
00:05:05,090 --> 00:05:09,050
On the upside, knowing exactly where the Grail will be is good for us.

57
00:05:09,050 --> 00:05:12,350
After all, our first priority is to stop its summoning.

58
00:05:12,350 --> 00:05:14,420
Saber will take the main gate.

59
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:17,290
She'll keep him occupied out front,

60
00:05:17,290 --> 00:05:21,480
and as she does, we'll climb the mountain from the back and destroy the Grail.

61
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:22,480
Hang on...

62
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:26,500
Isn't Saber the only one who can destroy it?

63
00:05:27,470 --> 00:05:28,490
Good point.

64
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:32,800
Once the Grail's summoned, we won't be able to destroy it.

65
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:36,950
But we can destroy its vessel before then.

66
00:05:36,950 --> 00:05:41,000
Basically, we shut down the Grail before it can activate.

67
00:05:41,470 --> 00:05:43,120
What do you mean?

68
00:05:43,120 --> 00:05:45,460
Judging by the events up until now,

69
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:48,260
you would assume the Holy Grail is Illyasviel's heart, right?

70
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:51,330
But I think it also needs her body—

71
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:54,520
or rather, magic circuits—to function.

72
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:58,140
He didn't want Illyasviel to become the Grail,

73
00:05:58,610 --> 00:06:01,150
so he only removed the core: her heart.

74
00:06:01,530 --> 00:06:05,140
Therefore, for it to function,

75
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:08,350
he needs to implant it into another mage's body.

76
00:06:09,190 --> 00:06:10,910
Since the two of us are here,

77
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:13,640
his choice for the Grail's foundation has to be...

78
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:16,010
Shinji?

79
00:06:16,010 --> 00:06:19,040
But he isn't, well...

80
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:23,550
Even if the Matou mage lineage has died out, 
they still have latent magic circuits.

81
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:28,520
Illyasviel's heart would forcibly open even those.

82
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:33,310
Which means that we have to start by locating Shinji.

83
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:39,560
Then I need to distract Archer until you two stop the Grail?

84
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:40,810
Yes.

85
00:06:40,810 --> 00:06:44,170
And as soon as we stop the Grail, we'll come running.

86
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:45,960
No, that's crazy.

87
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,940
Saber's no match for him.

88
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:51,020
On what grounds do you base that assessment, Shirou?

89
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:57,040
Uh... As a swordsman, he's no match for you,

90
00:06:57,380 --> 00:07:01,750
but no matter how skilled the warrior, they can't defeat war itself.

91
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:04,290
He's that kind of Heroic Spirit.

92
00:07:04,680 --> 00:07:08,830
You also have to be war itself, or you'll be swallowed whole.

93
00:07:08,830 --> 00:07:13,050
So you are saying that I would be at a disadvantage against him?

94
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:21,070
That's why we can't send Saber to fight him without a plan, Tohsaka.

95
00:07:21,070 --> 00:07:23,310
We need to figure out his weakness, at least.

96
00:07:23,730 --> 00:07:28,010
Like you said, his Noble Phantasm is war itself,

97
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:31,490
and on top of that, he's a Servant specialized in killing Heroic Spirits.

98
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:36,500
To beat him, you'd need to have an armory to equal his...

99
00:07:42,340 --> 00:07:43,510
What?

100
00:07:43,510 --> 00:07:45,540
Why did you stop mid-sentence?

101
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:48,130
I see.

102
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:51,150
That's why he always treated him like a sworn enemy.

103
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:55,140
Right, a Heroic Spirit without his own Noble Phantasm

104
00:07:55,770 --> 00:07:58,270
wouldn't have an original weapon.

105
00:07:59,140 --> 00:08:00,130
It'll work...

106
00:08:01,030 --> 00:08:02,140
This will work!

107
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:06,820
Hang on, that would mean...

108
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,460
If you have something to say, spit it out.

109
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:11,360
You have an idea, right?

110
00:08:11,360 --> 00:08:13,260
I do not!

111
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:16,030
I can't tell you here, you idiot!

112
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:19,040
Rin?

113
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:22,500
Anyway, the existing plan should be fine.

114
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:24,480
We carry it out before dawn, got it?

115
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:28,680
Until then, everyone should go to their rooms and get plenty of rest.

116
00:08:31,190 --> 00:08:34,590
Also, I need to discuss something with you, Saber.

117
00:08:43,830 --> 00:08:45,650
You're okay with this, Saber?

118
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:49,860
Yes. I think it the best option.

119
00:08:50,330 --> 00:08:51,710
You have my thanks, Rin.

120
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:56,240
This will allow me to fight without undue concern as well.

121
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:09,380
What do you want?

122
00:09:10,050 --> 00:09:11,650
What do I...

123
00:09:11,650 --> 00:09:15,380
Did I catch you in a really bad mood or something?

124
00:09:15,830 --> 00:09:19,460
No, not really. It's not like that.

125
00:09:19,460 --> 00:09:21,030
What's your problem, then?

126
00:09:21,030 --> 00:09:23,330
Do you have a fever or something?

127
00:09:23,330 --> 00:09:24,580
Of course I don't!

128
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:27,760
Jeez... Just come in already.

129
00:09:27,760 --> 00:09:30,260
Let me guess, you're here for another stupid reason?

130
00:09:39,970 --> 00:09:42,470
Tohsaka, what were you and Saber...

131
00:09:42,470 --> 00:09:43,960
What?

132
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:45,660
No, forget it.

133
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:49,190
Just hear me out and don't get mad.

134
00:09:49,190 --> 00:09:50,420
I want to—

135
00:09:50,420 --> 00:09:52,550
You want to fight him, don't you?

136
00:09:55,140 --> 00:09:58,340
Oh? So you figured it out.

137
00:09:58,340 --> 00:10:02,680
That the natural enemy of Gilgamesh's Noble Phantasm is Archer's magic.

138
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:04,660
It is?

139
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:06,710
Huh? Hang on...

140
00:10:06,710 --> 00:10:10,770
You came up with that hare-brained suggestion without even figuring that much out?

141
00:10:10,770 --> 00:10:15,900
No, I just had a gut feeling that I'd have the best chance out of the three of us.

142
00:10:17,770 --> 00:10:19,870
Well, your gut isn't wrong.

143
00:10:19,870 --> 00:10:24,570
What makes Gilgamesh the most powerful is the 
overwhelming number of Noble Phantasms he has.

144
00:10:24,570 --> 00:10:27,950
Furthermore, for every anti-Heroic-Spirit weapon there is, he has the original.

145
00:10:27,950 --> 00:10:32,030
But there is no Noble Phantasm legendary for killing Archer.

146
00:10:32,030 --> 00:10:36,820
Most of all, given sufficient mana, 
he could match anyone weapon for weapon.

147
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:42,150
Gilgamesh called you two "fakes,"

148
00:10:42,150 --> 00:10:46,010
but I'll bet that was because he actually saw you as threats.

149
00:10:46,010 --> 00:10:50,770
Because unlike others, he would have to fight Heroic Spirit Emiya on equal footing.

150
00:10:51,250 --> 00:10:52,890
There's a flaw in your plan, though.

151
00:10:52,890 --> 00:10:56,820
My projections won't be able to keep up with his barrage of Noble Phantasms,

152
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:58,440
and my mana won't last.

153
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:02,210
Yes, if your magic stays at its current level.

154
00:11:02,210 --> 00:11:05,500
But you remember Archer's Noble Phantasm, right?

155
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:06,950
If you could master that magic—

156
00:11:06,950 --> 00:11:12,460
that Reality Marble—you could hold your own against Gilgamesh.

157
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:13,930
That's crazy.

158
00:11:13,930 --> 00:11:15,800
I don't have that kind of mana.

159
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:19,670
Well, several options come to mind.

160
00:11:20,250 --> 00:11:21,970
But the one I'm thinking of...

161
00:11:21,970 --> 00:11:26,410
is a method that links two mages, along with their stores of mana.

162
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:36,270
You mean creating a path between you and me to share mana?

163
00:11:36,270 --> 00:11:37,080
Yes.

164
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:41,820
Even if you don't have the mana to use a Reality Marble, I do.

165
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:47,060
I'll have you use my mana to fight Gilgamesh.

166
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:50,870
Now, as for how to establish that path...

167
00:11:54,660 --> 00:11:55,620
Tohsaka?

168
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:04,720
I'm going to transplant my magic crest onto you.

169
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:07,990
But isn't that...

170
00:12:07,990 --> 00:12:11,720
Isn't the magic crest considered a mage's ultimate legacy?

171
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:13,310
That's right.

172
00:12:13,310 --> 00:12:19,080
The current family head takes magic that was originally formless and shapes it over the course of their life.

173
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:22,610
It's the heritage of a mage family, 
handed down from generation to generation.

174
00:12:23,570 --> 00:12:26,120
I can't take something that means so much to you.

175
00:12:27,230 --> 00:12:28,500
It's fine.

176
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:30,680
This is my most important fight,

177
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:33,120
so I have to commit my most important possession, right?

178
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:38,630
Why are you staring at me like that?

179
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:41,730
Sorry. I was just in awe of you for a second.

180
00:12:41,730 --> 00:12:46,800
I know it's kinda late to say this, 
but that's what made me fall for you.

181
00:12:47,380 --> 00:12:49,050
F-Fall for me?

182
00:12:49,050 --> 00:12:52,100
This is hardly the time for sweet talk!

183
00:12:52,100 --> 00:12:55,730
But if you want to keep going, 
I guess I could force myself to listen.

184
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:58,070
Yeah, I know.

185
00:12:58,070 --> 00:12:59,480
There's not much time.

186
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:02,810
Okay, let's start the transplant.

187
00:13:02,810 --> 00:13:05,570
What do you need me to do, Tohsaka?

188
00:13:08,910 --> 00:13:11,910
Well, start by getting undressed...

189
00:13:18,090 --> 00:13:18,920
What's wrong?

190
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:21,640
Look, don't get any funny ideas!

191
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:24,670
I only said to take your clothes off, got it?

192
00:13:24,670 --> 00:13:27,550
I'm taking mine off too, so it's all fair.

193
00:13:28,630 --> 00:13:30,390
You're undressing too?

194
00:13:30,390 --> 00:13:33,430
L-Like I said, don't get the wrong idea!

195
00:13:33,430 --> 00:13:36,640
Getting undressed is to facilitate the transfer of body heat.

196
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:38,920
That's all there is to it!

197
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:41,930
Listen. To transplant a magic crest,

198
00:13:41,930 --> 00:13:44,870
we need to enter a state of deep rapport.

199
00:13:44,870 --> 00:13:46,780
Oh, I get it.

200
00:13:47,430 --> 00:13:49,660
Um, just my top is okay, right?

201
00:13:52,160 --> 00:13:54,290
Obviously!

202
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:12,310
I'm going to begin.

203
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,420
Tohsaka!

204
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:50,880
Did it work?

205
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:55,640
Tohsaka?

206
00:16:55,640 --> 00:16:58,200
Of course it worked.

207
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:00,450
It was so flawless there's nothing to critique.

208
00:17:00,450 --> 00:17:03,230
So precise there won't be any aftereffects.

209
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:05,970
So perfect that even Kirei, who specialized in this stuff,

210
00:17:05,970 --> 00:17:09,620
would compliment me and say, 
"That was fine work, my disciple."

211
00:17:11,410 --> 00:17:12,720
So this is...

212
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:13,790
Yes.

213
00:17:13,790 --> 00:17:16,490
It's the magic crest I transplanted onto you.

214
00:17:16,490 --> 00:17:20,860
This will give you more than enough mana to create a Reality Marble.

215
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:21,830
So the rest...

216
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:24,280
That's up to me.

217
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:26,210
Thanks, Tohsaka.

218
00:17:28,770 --> 00:17:32,210
But why are you so angry?

219
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:34,880
You saw it, didn't you?

220
00:17:36,090 --> 00:17:39,270
Hang on, did I do something?

221
00:17:39,270 --> 00:17:42,330
You saw it, didn't you? You brute!

222
00:17:42,330 --> 00:17:45,000
I don't know what you're talking about, but I'm sure you're wrong!

223
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,840
My eyes were closed the whole time,

224
00:17:46,840 --> 00:17:50,310
and the only thing I saw were some images that looked like magic circuits...

225
00:17:52,210 --> 00:17:53,830
Ah, right, Tohsaka.

226
00:17:53,830 --> 00:17:55,720
There was that weird dream...

227
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:58,330
Like I was in a schoolyard somewhere,

228
00:17:58,330 --> 00:18:03,160
watching some guy doing high jumps like an idiot until the sun set.

229
00:18:04,810 --> 00:18:06,230
What the heck was...

230
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:10,170
What was that for?

231
00:18:10,170 --> 00:18:13,540
Shut up, shut up, shut up, shut up!

232
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:15,510
Shut up, shut up!

233
00:18:14,120 --> 00:18:17,280
Don't be so rough on the pillows, you idiot!

234
00:18:19,150 --> 00:18:20,920
Shut up, you brute!

235
00:18:20,920 --> 00:18:24,560
Don't peek at other people's secrets and then act all high and mighty!

236
00:18:24,950 --> 00:18:28,150
Huh? You call that a secret?

237
00:18:30,210 --> 00:18:31,250
Fine, whatever.

238
00:18:31,250 --> 00:18:34,750
I'll get a look at your embarrassing memories sooner or later!

239
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:38,280
And when I do, I won't hold back, you hear?!

240
00:19:22,570 --> 00:19:25,080
What are you doing, Saber?

241
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:28,250
A great many things have happened.

242
00:19:29,840 --> 00:19:34,520
I wished to etch them into my mind, so that I might never forget them.

243
00:19:35,860 --> 00:19:36,920
I see.

244
00:19:38,900 --> 00:19:41,590
If you can, I hope you always remember.

245
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:47,690
I shall.

246
00:19:49,550 --> 00:19:52,240
Also, I must give you my thanks.

247
00:19:53,200 --> 00:19:54,530
Thank you, Shirou.

248
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:57,870
It took quite some time,

249
00:19:57,870 --> 00:20:01,360
but you have shown me the way.

250
00:20:02,220 --> 00:20:03,610
Saber?

251
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:08,000
Forgive me. This surely makes no sense to you.

252
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,340
But I wished to put it into words.

253
00:20:11,340 --> 00:20:13,620
One dream has come to an end.

254
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:17,580
Although I was unable to leave you any example to follow,

255
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:21,380
you have given me an answer that is more than sufficient.

256
00:20:22,200 --> 00:20:23,700
A dream?

257
00:20:23,700 --> 00:20:25,890
You mean yours?

258
00:20:25,890 --> 00:20:27,440
I cannot say.

259
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:31,730
Even if it is mine, it is the story of an unknown little girl—

260
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:34,060
one who no longer has anything to do with me.

261
00:20:36,330 --> 00:20:38,790
I once had a dream.

262
00:20:43,740 --> 00:20:46,570
I have a favor to ask of you as well.

263
00:20:46,570 --> 00:20:48,940
I shall protect the two of you.

264
00:20:48,940 --> 00:20:53,250
So make certain that you both return to this house.

265
00:20:54,140 --> 00:20:56,700
Sure, we'll come back here.

266
00:20:56,700 --> 00:20:57,720
You can count on it.

267
00:21:03,980 --> 00:21:06,530
Let's go settle this once and for all, Saber.

268
00:21:41,210 --> 00:21:44,550
Vomit forth your curses, Holy Grail.

269
00:21:45,010 --> 00:21:51,560
The time has come to judge whether the humans of this era

270
00:21:51,970 --> 00:21:55,060
can withstand the weight of their own wishes.

271
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:28,890
We'll put an end to your Holy Grail right now!

272
00:23:28,890 --> 00:23:31,780
With Caster gone, you should not still be here!

273
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:34,670
I'm not good enough to fend off his Noble Phantasms.

274
00:23:34,670 --> 00:23:36,710
You filthy sham.

275
00:23:36,710 --> 00:23:40,590
Learn firsthand the difference 
between counterfeits and the real thing!

276
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:21,910
Gib dem wandernden Vogel das Trinkwasser,

277
00:14:21,910 --> 00:14:24,180
der vom langen Weg kommt.

278
00:14:24,180 --> 00:14:26,050
Benutz den Vogelrahmen

279
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:31,040
in dem der Schlüssel nicht angewendet wird.

280
00:14:31,870 --> 00:14:36,900
Ich spinne den Regenbogen in neuem selbst.

281
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:39,210
Heißes Wetter, Regen,

282
00:14:39,210 --> 00:14:43,710
Wind, Schnee, Krieg, Ende, ununterbrochen.

283
00:14:43,710 --> 00:14:49,720
Nimm an, ohne anderer Meinung zu sein, ohne zu fallen.

284
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:52,880
Es nimmt an, ohne zu fürchten,

285
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:54,970
ohne zu zweifeln.

286
00:14:56,600 --> 00:15:02,150
Sieg im Freund, der auf eine Reise entfernt geht.

